    <div class="article-body reveal">

      <p>This Cookie Policy explains how Zennly (&ldquo;Zennly&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;, or &ldquo;our&rdquo;), operated by Zunkireelabs, uses cookies and similar technologies on <a href="{{ site.url }}/">zennly.io</a>. It should be read together with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your device when you visit it. They help a website work, remember your choices and understand how it is used. Similar technologies, such as local storage and tracking pixels, work in much the same way, and we refer to all of them as &ldquo;cookies&rdquo; in this policy.</p>

      <h2>2. How we use cookies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> &ndash; needed for the Zennly platform to work, for example to keep you signed in to your account and to keep your session secure. These cannot be switched off in our systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> &ndash; used to understand how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited and how people reach us, so that we can improve it.</li>
        <li><strong>Third-party content</strong> &ndash; some content on our website is loaded from other providers, described in Section 3.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not run advertising or retargeting tags on this website at the time of writing.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and services we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics (GA4)</strong> &ndash; sets cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which distinguish visitors and sessions and typically last up to two years. Google processes this data to give us aggregated reports on website usage. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google&rsquo;s cookie information</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> &ndash; our pages load fonts from Google&rsquo;s servers. Google may receive your IP address and browser information when the fonts are requested.</li>
        <li><strong>Calendly</strong> &ndash; on our demo page, you can open Calendly to book a time. Calendly may set its own cookies when you use its booking widget. See <a href="https://calendly.com/legal/cookie-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Calendly&rsquo;s cookie policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Image hosting</strong> &ndash; some images on our website are loaded from third-party image services, which may receive your IP address and browser information.</li>
        <li><strong>The Zennly platform</strong> &ndash; when you sign in to your account, we use essential cookies or similar storage to keep you signed in and to remember your preferences.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How to control cookies</h2>
      <p>You can control and delete cookies through your browser settings; the help pages for your browser explain how. Disabling cookies may affect some functions of our website or platform, and signing in may not work without essential cookies.</p>
      <p>To opt out of Google Analytics across websites, you can install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>

      <h2>5. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time, for example if we change the services we use. We will post the updated version on this page with a revised &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date.</p>

      <h2>6. Contact us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about how we use cookies, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@zennly.io">info@zennly.io</a>.</p>

